    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, your software subscriptions and new desk would follow the same rules as your ergonomic chair. Both are considered capital expenses and should be depreciated over their useful life. For software subscriptions, you can typically deduct the full cost in the year you purchase them, as long as they are used exclusively for business purposes.\n\nRegarding your lost or misplaced receipts, it's always best to keep them organized, but it's not necessarily a huge problem for an audit. The IRS generally expects you to keep receipts for a reasonable period, usually three to seven years. If you can't find them, you can still file your taxes, but you may need to estimate the expenses or provide a reasonable explanation. It's always better to have a good record-keeping system in place to avoid such situations, much like a goblin would keep track of their shiny trinkets and treasures. If you're concerned, you might want to consult with a tax professional to ensure everything is in order.",
